<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The mark on its disc, with no ground behind it.

  This is what Android 12's splash screen draws. `Theme.SplashScreen` composes
  the launch window from `windowSplashScreenBackground` and
  `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon`; it ignores a theme's window background
  entirely, which is why `contour_splash.xml` — carefully hand-built so the
  disc matched the app's own — was never reached on any modern phone. What
  showed instead was the launcher icon on Android's default ground: the square
  logo on the wrong colour, one frame before the app drew the circular one.

  The disc fills this drawable deliberately, and so renders at whatever size
  the system's icon canvas is — measured at 188dp on a Galaxy S24. Declaring a
  larger canvas here to make the disc come out at 112dp was tried and changed
  nothing at all on that phone, which is the evidence that One UI is drawing
  the launcher icon rather than this file. Since both routes land on the same
  ~192dp, the app's own splash is sized to match it instead; see
  `SPLASH_DISC_PX` in `packages/ui/src/lock-timing.ts`.

  The icon is drawn into a fixed canvas and then circle-masked. Without an
  icon background colour that canvas is 288dp with the inner 192dp visible —
  `core-splashscreen`'s own `splashscreen_icon_size_no_background` (288dp) and
  its 410dp mask with a 109dp stroke, which leaves 192dp. So a disc declared
  here at `contour_mark_disc` renders at that many dp, and the 112dp the web
  splash and the lock screen use fits inside the mask with room to spare.

  `@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground` rather than `ic_launcher_round`: the round
  one is an `adaptive-icon` on API 26+, which is XML and not a bitmap. The
  reasoning is in `contour_splash.xml`, which now composes this file.

  The mark is sized here rather than inherited from the asset. It used to carry
  its own inset, which put it at 52% of this disc while the lock screen drew
  the same mark at 86% of the same disc — so it grew at the handover, on the
  one screen whose whole job is to not change.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:width="@dimen/contour_mark_disc"
        android:height="@dimen/contour_mark_disc"
        android:gravity="center">
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="@color/contour_blue" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <item
        android:width="@dimen/contour_mark"
        android:height="@dimen/contour_mark"
        android:gravity="center">
        <bitmap
            android:src="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"
            android:gravity="center" />
    </item>
</layer-list>
